      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm really sorry to hear you're feeling this way. It's important to check your blood sugar immediately and follow your diabetes care plan. If your sugar is low, consuming fast-acting carbohydrates such as glucose tablets, juice, or candy can help raise it quickly. However, consult your healthcare provider before making any changes to your insulin regimen. They can help ensure your treatment stays on track and safe. Stay calm and take a moment to grab something to address your sugar levels.",
